<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.930 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.930 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE JULY 31, 1999</p>
<p>			     $15.515 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	5.930    Awarded At	99.898	5.875</p>
<p> MEDIAN    0.000    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 0.000    99 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.53 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Jul.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Jul.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 22.Jun.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  15.515 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128273B6</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   39.208			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.040				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 5.875</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  878.00 MLN		     PRICE	 99.898</p>
